{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 recorded below-seam ambient config/credential reads across the reconciler PASS CORE as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`; the in-process AST gate `check_config_ownership.py` still flags them. Sibling C3a-JIRA (a34b) owns the disjoint adapters/** + access_check.py surface, so no conflict.\n\nThe 45 flagged reads (all flagged when drained — none already-owned):\n- **`REBAR_ROOT` (12)** — uniform `Path(os.environ.get(\"REBAR_ROOT\") or …parents[4])`; **`load_config` (17)** — ambient `rebar.config.load_config()` (both enumerated in clusters 1/2).\n- **dynamic `os.environ.get` (7)** — dead/toggle-only `_rebar_env`/`_env_int` wrapper bodies (`apply_handlers`, `apply_inbound`, `binding_store`, `inbound_translate`, `outbound_differ`×2, `rebar_id_audit`, `bridge_fsck_visibility`).\n- **identity (3)**: `REBAR_ENV_ID` (`inbound_translate`, `last_pass`×2), `REBAR_AUTHOR` (`inbound_translate`). **tuning (2)**: `RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE` (`binding_store`, `binding_walk`). **toggles (4)**: see allowlist.\n\nAffected SOURCE: the modules above + `src/rebar/config.py` (resolvers) + `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` (removes 45 rows). Affected TEST consumers (updated in-scope; run in regression): the `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` toggle suites (`apply/test_silent_noop_canary.py`, `conflict/test_conflict_filing_deferred.py`), the `test_identity_*` suites, `conftest.py`, and binding tests setting `RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE`.\n\n## Outcome\nONE architectural cutover. The reconciler already composes ONE immutable `ReconcilerRuntime` per pass (`compose_reconciler_runtime` → `_operation_config.compose_operation_snapshot`, threaded via `_PassContext` in `reconcile.reconcile_once`). This slice extends that seam to compose root + typed `Config` ONCE and thread them down, replacing every below-seam ambient read; each read gets one treatment and its `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` row removed. Portability: the gate is in-process AST (no CI-provider trigger). No stored-format changes (pure routing/threading; rollback = revert).\n\n## Decision rule\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (default; 41 reads).** A read whose value is composed config/root is resolved ONCE through an owned `config.py`/`_config_sources.py` resolver and THREADED into the below-seam helper; the ambient read no longer exists. **Timing:** these values are stable for the whole pass, so compose-once-and-thread is correct; reads resolved LIVE per operation stay owned-in-place (b) so a mid-operation override is never lost.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via `# read-via:` marker.** A read that is NOT composed config — a kill-switch, failure-injection toggle, or per-operation override — keeps a `# read-via:` marker naming the category. CAPPED at the 4 reads below = exactly **6 marked lines** (the gate flags each LINE); nothing else is marked.\n\n### Owned-in-place allowlist (4 reads = 6 marked lines — the cap)\n1. `__main__.py L274` `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_STEAL` — kill-switch (default ON; OFF = old unconditional exit-3). 1 line.\n2. `reconcile_helpers.py L629` `REBAR_RECONCILER_WRITE_FACADE` — AC6 rollback toggle. 1 line.\n3. `apply_handlers.py L184/424/462` `REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP` — failure-injection test toggle, read live; inlined to direct marked `os.environ.get` (deleting its `_rebar_env` wrapper clears the paired row). 3 lines.\n4. `apply_inbound.py L244` `REBAR_RECONCILER_CONFLICT_PARENT_ID` — per-conflict operator override (default `\"\"`), read live; inlined to direct marked `os.environ.get` (deleting its `_rebar_env` wrapper clears the paired row). 1 line.\n\n## The cut, by cluster\n**Owned resolution (composition roots `config.py`/`_config_sources.py`):** REUSE the existing owned `rebar.config.repo_root` (= `_config_sources.repo_root`, explicit > `REBAR_ROOT` > git-top > cwd — the function `compose_operation_snapshot` already delegates to; no duplicate). Reuse landed `compose_config()`. ADD `config.resolve_absent_retire_grace()` (raw env > default, clamp ≥ 1; no `cfg` param — a raw env knob, not a typed key). The three DISTINCT `REBAR_ENV_ID`/`REBAR_AUTHOR` reads are NOT unified — three owned accessors, one per call site, each verbatim (below).\n\n- **cluster 1 — `REBAR_ROOT` (12):** entrypoints (`__main__`, `reconcile`, `request`) call the existing owned `rebar.config.repo_root()`; the composed root threads via `_PassContext.repo_root` to `applier`, `apply_inbound`, `apply_planning`, `dispatch_one`, `fetcher`, `inbound_translate`, `invariants`, `pass_io`, `_engine_support/reads`.\n- **cluster 2 — `load_config` (17):** the composed `Config` (+ runtime backend for the `select_backend` sites) threads into the 14 reconciler modules + `_engine_support/gates`,`lookups`,`reads` carrying the drained `load_config` rows; each reads its typed field (`sync.remote`, `deletion_probe_limit`, `id_guard_bypass_unsafe`, …).\n- **identity (3) — three per-call-site owned accessors, NOT unified, each verbatim:** (i) `last_pass.resolve_environment_id` L71 keeps its 3-tier `explicit > REBAR_ENV_ID(set-but-empty→error) > .env-id file→`local:`-prefix` — the env read moves to an owned accessor, `last_pass` re-raises as `LastPassError`; (ii) `last_pass` L329 keeps its None-able raw passthrough to `publish()` via owned `config.environment_id_or_none()` (no default/error); (iii) `inbound_translate` L174/175 keep default-when-UNSET via owned `config.reconciler_event_identity()`→`(env_id, author)` with `LEGACY_JIRA_*` defaults (empty→`''`, never raises), deleting the `_rebar_env` wrapper.\n- **tuning (2):** `config.resolve_absent_retire_grace()` threads into `binding_store`/`binding_walk` (deleting ambient `_env_int`/`_resolve_grace`).\n- **dead/rewired dynamic reads:** the `_rebar_env`/`_env_int` wrappers in `outbound_differ`, `rebar_id_audit` (and the toggle-only ones post-inline) are unused → DELETED, clearing their `os.environ.get` rows (not marked). `bridge_fsck_visibility`'s injected `env` seam is made required from the composed context, dropping the ambient fallback.\n- Remove the 45 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows.\n**Shared-helper re-derivation (Serena `find_referencing_symbols`):** `_engine_support/reads.py`, `lookups.py`, `gates.py` have CLI/MCP callers outside the pass → signatures UNCHANGED, the ambient read becomes an INTERNAL delegation to the owned resolver. Pass-internal helpers RECEIVE the threaded value (in-pass call sites re-derived via Serena).\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\nHeld-out `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_core_seam_clean_heldout.py` (imports the gate by bare name `import check_config_ownership`) asserts: (i) `check(REPO_ROOT)` has no finding for any listed path; (ii) `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has zero entries for a listed file; (iii) `# read-via:` markers across those files total exactly **6** — `__main__.py` (1), `reconcile_helpers.py` (1), `apply_handlers.py` (3), `apply_inbound.py` (1), every other file 0. RED now. A timing regression asserts `FAIL_SILENT_NOOP`/`CONFLICT_PARENT_ID` set mid-operation are still observed live. Regression green: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/**`, the `tests/interfaces`/`integration` reconciler paths, and the consumers above.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No ambient config/credential read remains below the seam in the 41 listed files: each is cut-to-seam (41) or one of the 4 owned-in-place reads (6 marked lines); no other read marked; live per-operation reads stay owned-in-place, not compose-once.\n- [ ] The 45 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows are removed and `check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out marker-total==6 / per-file check).\n- [ ] Root + typed `Config` are composed ONCE at the entrypoint and threaded through `_PassContext`/helper signatures; the three identity reads keep distinct per-call-site semantics; shared `_engine_support` helpers resolve internally (signatures unchanged).\n- [ ] Regression suites in Testing pass; provider-neutral outcomes unchanged except deltas recorded as a comment."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787108826019231001,"uuid":"fd3ae2f3-3404-4944-b696-bace878e80f8"}